  "id": "COMPOUND:15797 - PROTEIN:1493",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Coumanolignan may interact with the Prostaglandin E2 receptor EP4 subtype through multiple pathways. The drug-target relationship is supported by the presence of Coumanolignan as a target of several compounds, including 4-[(6,7-Dimethoxy-2-Methyl-3,4-Dihydro-1H-Isoquinolin-1-Yl)Methyl]Phenol and Anhydrofurospongin-1, both of which are known to target the EP4 subtype. Additionally, Coumanolignan is also linked to Fusion glycoprotein F0, which is itself a target of cis-Isopinocamphone, another compound that interacts with the EP4 receptor. These findings collectively indicate that Coumanolignan may exert its biological effects through a network of molecular interactions that ultimately modulate the activity of the Prostaglandin E2 receptor EP4 subtype. The evidence is consistent with a mechanism involving the modulation of receptor function, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
